  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44129706",
      "title": "Template-driven: Registering Form Controls",
      "lectureOrder": 243,
      "videoOrder": 231,
      "sourceHash": "173167215e4236c338ce4055f007f00ffad85ee8bfc677b66fbdffeb3bb1f340",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 2.34,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmuller] So let's now manage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.34,
          "end": 7.14,
          "en": "this form here with help of template-driven forms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.14,
          "end": 9.57,
          "en": "And for that, in this starting project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.57,
          "end": 13.77,
          "en": "I'll go to the login.component in that auth folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.77,
          "end": 17.82,
          "en": "because it's in that component that this form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.82,
          "end": 20.73,
          "en": "which we see on the screen here, is set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.73,
          "end": 24.903,
          "en": "or that the markup for this form is set up, I should say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.92,
          "end": 28.77,
          "en": "Because at the moment, this markup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.77,
          "end": 33.36,
          "en": "and also this login.component does not include any code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.36,
          "end": 36.21,
          "en": "that would handle any user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.21,
          "end": 39.18,
          "en": "And that's of course ultimately what we wanna do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.18,
          "end": 40.77,
          "en": "though as you'll see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.77,
          "end": 43.86,
          "en": "we'll actually do a bit more than that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.86,
          "end": 46.14,
          "en": "We'll actually also make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.14,
          "end": 49.77,
          "en": "that we tell the user about errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.77,
          "end": 52.65,
          "en": "that we validate the user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.65,
          "end": 55.44,
          "en": "and some other things as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.44,
          "end": 56.7,
          "en": "Now, as I mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 56.7,
          "end": 60.6,
          "en": "I wanna start by managing this form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.6,
          "end": 64.71,
          "en": "with this template-driven forms approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.71,
          "end": 67.71,
          "en": "And in the end, this approach, as you will see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.71,
          "end": 69.42,
          "en": "is kind of related",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.42,
          "end": 74.25,
          "en": "to how we managed form submissions thus far.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.25,
          "end": 76.44,
          "en": "You'll see some similarities there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.44,
          "end": 78.36,
          "en": "but you'll now understand how some",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.36,
          "end": 80.64,
          "en": "of these features work together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.64,
          "end": 83.01,
          "en": "Because when it comes to managing a form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.01,
          "end": 86.19,
          "en": "with this template-driven forms approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.19,
          "end": 88.86,
          "en": "it all starts here in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.86,
          "end": 91.38,
          "en": "Because when using this approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.38,
          "end": 95.22,
          "en": "you let Angular know about your form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.22,
          "end": 99.09,
          "en": "and the input elements by adding special directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.09,
          "end": 102.84,
          "en": "to some of these elements in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.84,
          "end": 105.87,
          "en": "And that's also important to understand here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.87,
          "end": 110.87,
          "en": "The end goal is to make Angular aware of this form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.57,
          "end": 115.14,
          "en": "and its inputs so that you can then use Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.14,
          "end": 117.47999999999999,
          "en": "and some features it offers to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.47999999999999,
          "end": 120.51,
          "en": "to easily interact with this form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.51,
          "end": 123.66,
          "en": "And for example, extract the entered values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.66,
          "end": 126.18299999999999,
          "en": "but also some other pieces of information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.83,
          "end": 130.53,
          "en": "And therefore, let's start by making Angular aware",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.53,
          "end": 133.623,
          "en": "of this email input field, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.91,
          "end": 136.29,
          "en": "And you would do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.29,
          "end": 140.07,
          "en": "by adding a directive onto this input element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.07,
          "end": 144.87,
          "en": "a directive which you already know, the ngModel directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.87,
          "end": 148.173,
          "en": "But here, without two-way binding,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.25,
          "end": 152.57999999999998,
          "en": "we could use two-way binding if we wanted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.57999999999998,
          "end": 156.72,
          "en": "to two-way bind this input if we wanted to be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.72,
          "end": 159.87,
          "en": "to override the value entered there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.87,
          "end": 161.61,
          "en": "with help of two-way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.61,
          "end": 166.61,
          "en": "But you don't have to use ngModel with two-way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.74,
          "end": 169.26,
          "en": "And that's of course something new,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 169.26,
          "end": 172.2,
          "en": "which we haven't done thus far.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.2,
          "end": 174.09,
          "en": "Because up to this point in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 174.09,
          "end": 177.06,
          "en": "we always used ngModel with two-way binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 177.06,
          "end": 180.21,
          "en": "But it turns out that you don't have to use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 180.21,
          "end": 182.34,
          "en": "with two-way binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 182.34,
          "end": 184.86,
          "en": "because this ngModel directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 184.86,
          "end": 189.86,
          "en": "in the end, registers an input element with Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 190.83,
          "end": 192.9,
          "en": "And an input element doesn't have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 192.9,
          "end": 195.36,
          "en": "to be an input element as it's here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 195.36,
          "end": 199.32,
          "en": "It could also be a text area or a select element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 199.32,
          "end": 200.91,
          "en": "or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 200.91,
          "end": 204.6,
          "en": "So any kind of HTML input element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 204.6,
          "end": 208.503,
          "en": "any HTML element that is about gathering user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 209.94,
          "end": 214.68,
          "en": "So ngModel registers this element with Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 214.68,
          "end": 217.82999999999998,
          "en": "It makes Angular aware of this input element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 217.82999999999998,
          "end": 221.16,
          "en": "and it allows Angular to manage it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 221.16,
          "end": 222.99,
          "en": "behind the scenes, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 222.99,
          "end": 226.98,
          "en": "And it will also allow you to gain access to that element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 226.98,
          "end": 228.393,
          "en": "as I'll soon show you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 229.74,
          "end": 233.49,
          "en": "Now, in order to make ngModel work here though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 233.49,
          "end": 237.18,
          "en": "we have to go to the login.component TypeScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 237.18,
          "end": 240.24,
          "en": "and add the imports array there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 240.24,
          "end": 242.94,
          "en": "because just as before in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 242.94,
          "end": 245.28,
          "en": "in order to make ngModel work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 245.28,
          "end": 249.183,
          "en": "you should add the FormsModule to this imports array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 250.14,
          "end": 253.35,
          "en": "Because this will unlock this ngModel directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 253.35,
          "end": 256.323,
          "en": "and some other form related features as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 257.94,
          "end": 262.56,
          "en": "So with that done, you can go back to your website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 262.56,
          "end": 265.29,
          "en": "and there you'll find an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 265.29,
          "end": 267.84,
          "en": "in the developer tools console",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 267.84,
          "end": 268.863,
          "en": "if you open that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.3,
          "end": 271.92,
          "en": "There you'll find the error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 271.92,
          "end": 275.34000000000003,
          "en": "that ngModel must be used within a form tag,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 275.34000000000003,
          "end": 278.1,
          "en": "and then it must be used on an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 278.1,
          "end": 280.803,
          "en": "that has the name attribute set on it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 282.36,
          "end": 284.67,
          "en": "And currently, that's not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 284.67,
          "end": 286.23,
          "en": "I am in a form element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 286.23,
          "end": 287.7,
          "en": "but this input element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 287.7,
          "end": 290.943,
          "en": "doesn't have the name attribute set on it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 291.78,
          "end": 293.97,
          "en": "So that's something we have to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 293.97,
          "end": 297.15,
          "en": "And I deliberately did not do that in advance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 297.15,
          "end": 299.76,
          "en": "so that you really understand this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 299.76,
          "end": 304.17,
          "en": "and memorize this fact that you must add the name attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 304.17,
          "end": 307.68,
          "en": "to elements that do use ngModel",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 307.68,
          "end": 310.98,
          "en": "because it's this name that will then internally be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 310.98,
          "end": 315.06,
          "en": "by Angular to register this input element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 315.06,
          "end": 316.773,
          "en": "and to manage it, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 317.82,
          "end": 319.05,
          "en": "The name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 319.05,
          "end": 320.49,
          "en": "And here, I'll choose email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 320.49,
          "end": 323.013,
          "en": "since that makes sense for this input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 324.51,
          "end": 326.04,
          "en": "With that name added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 326.04,
          "end": 329.283,
          "en": "if I save this, this error goes away though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 330.69,
          "end": 332.61,
          "en": "And with that, we now registered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 332.61,
          "end": 336.09000000000003,
          "en": "this first input with Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 336.09000000000003,
          "end": 339.063,
          "en": "Now of course, we can do the same for the second input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 340.11,
          "end": 342.573,
          "en": "and I'll give this a name of password here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 345.51,
          "end": 348.24,
          "en": "but what's now the advantage of doing that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 348.24,
          "end": 352.02,
          "en": "How does ngModel now allow us to get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 352.02,
          "end": 355.32,
          "en": "to these input elements and learn more about them?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 355.32,
          "end": 358.383,
          "en": "Well, that's what we'll take care of in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
